WEBVTT

00:41.416 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:44.962 --> 00:47.089
Sis, I found a way!

00:47.172 --> 00:49.132
It's going to take some time,

00:49.216 --> 00:52.052
but I found a way for you to turn back

00:52.135 --> 00:53.804
into a nine-tailed fox.

00:53.887 --> 00:56.765
Okay, let's talk about it later.

00:57.432 --> 01:01.186
That means he can
go back to his life too, right?

01:02.980 --> 01:04.356
Wait a second.

01:05.274 --> 01:08.402
What are you guys talking about?

01:11.822 --> 01:13.991
Woo-seok, the thing is--

01:14.074 --> 01:16.076
Turning back into a nine-tailed fox?

01:17.911 --> 01:19.496
Then that means…

01:24.167 --> 01:29.381
You weren't actually doing this for me.
You just couldn't go back?

01:29.464 --> 01:30.924
Well…

01:31.883 --> 01:33.927
- Let me explain--
- That's right.

01:34.595 --> 01:36.513
It's exactly as you heard.

01:36.597 --> 01:38.390
So what? What's it to you?

01:38.473 --> 01:40.934
- Hey!
- Nothing's going to change anyway.

01:41.018 --> 01:42.894
Me, Si-yeol, and you.

01:42.978 --> 01:45.522
We're all going back
to the way things were.

01:46.148 --> 01:47.608
It'll just take a little more time.

01:49.693 --> 01:50.819
Really?

01:54.239 --> 01:55.365
How much longer?

02:00.537 --> 02:04.666
So you're saying you're human now,
just like the rest of us?

02:05.375 --> 02:07.711
And you're looking for a way back, right?

02:11.965 --> 02:14.217
So you found a way? How?

02:14.301 --> 02:18.055
Now that useless human's involved,
this all just got a lot more complicated.

02:19.598 --> 02:22.893
So there's a chance we can't switch back
if that method doesn't work?

02:22.976 --> 02:26.104
Well, that is a possibility.

02:26.188 --> 02:27.898
Why the hell do you care?

02:27.981 --> 02:29.650
This matters to me as well.

02:30.776 --> 02:33.362
Why?
Are you afraid I might get in the way?

02:34.821 --> 02:36.239
You tell me.

02:36.323 --> 02:38.325
I think you're fully capable of that.

02:39.076 --> 02:41.787
So tell me.
Are you going to get in the way?

02:46.166 --> 02:47.668
Stop it, both of you.

02:47.751 --> 02:48.919
Why are you acting like this?

02:49.878 --> 02:52.547
You heard what he said, didn't you?

02:52.631 --> 02:56.718
Don't tell me you're still clinging
to the idea of human friendships.

02:57.344 --> 02:59.971
- You're just being too harsh.
- Si-yeol.

03:00.055 --> 03:02.933
I need to know what's going on.
Otherwise I can't relax.

03:03.016 --> 03:05.936
And there might be something
I can do to help.

03:06.019 --> 03:08.730
You shouldn't just hide everything
from me like this.

03:08.814 --> 03:10.649
I understand what you're saying.

03:11.274 --> 03:13.151
Still, it would be best
if you left for now.

03:13.235 --> 03:15.654
- Later, if I need--
- Erase it.

03:16.571 --> 03:17.948
Pardon?

03:18.031 --> 03:19.449
Erase that human's memory.

03:19.533 --> 03:22.577
But my spiritual power isn't that strong--

03:22.661 --> 03:25.706
I know. Just do it.

03:25.789 --> 03:26.790
Okay.

03:27.874 --> 03:29.167
No, wait--

03:42.806 --> 03:43.974
What the…

03:44.975 --> 03:46.977
I was just waiting for Si-yeol.

03:47.978 --> 03:49.146
Why am I here?

03:53.358 --> 03:55.068
DAD

03:56.278 --> 03:57.320
Hi, Dad.

03:57.404 --> 03:59.489
Why are you just picking up now?

04:00.323 --> 04:01.867
I can't really remember right now--

04:01.950 --> 04:04.411
Have you been drinking
at a time like this?

04:04.494 --> 04:05.579
No, it's not that--

04:05.662 --> 04:08.206
Do you know what kind of mess you caused?

04:08.290 --> 04:10.292
You went to Korea
without the club's permission.

04:10.375 --> 04:12.043
Are you out of your mind?

04:14.629 --> 04:16.131
It's the preseason right now.

04:16.214 --> 04:18.258
I've got the international call-up
next week anyway.

04:18.341 --> 04:20.051
I just came to Korea a few days early.

04:20.135 --> 04:21.678
What's the big deal?

04:21.762 --> 04:24.931
You've still got training,
even in preseason!

04:25.015 --> 04:26.433
You just transferred,

04:26.516 --> 04:29.519
and you've already upset the coach
and the club owner.

04:29.603 --> 04:31.730
You're being unprofessional!

04:31.813 --> 04:33.482
Do you think I'm doing this for myself?

04:33.565 --> 04:34.941
What?

04:35.025 --> 04:37.194
Forget it. I'm hanging up.

04:39.696 --> 04:40.947
Let's keep it like this…

04:41.990 --> 04:43.450
for now.

04:44.284 --> 04:45.827
Thank you, Si-yeol.

04:47.537 --> 04:50.040
Wait, what was that memory just now?

04:52.751 --> 04:54.419
Did I actually meet Si-yeol?

04:54.961 --> 04:56.213
By the way,

04:56.838 --> 04:58.173
where is the house?

04:59.382 --> 05:00.884
It's right here.

05:03.136 --> 05:04.679
Isn't this a public restroom?

05:04.763 --> 05:06.932
There are lots of these in the mountains.

05:10.352 --> 05:13.438
This isn't a restroom.
It's what we call a rooftop apartment.

05:15.357 --> 05:19.528
It might not look like it,
but people actually live here.

05:19.611 --> 05:21.071
It's a home.

05:21.154 --> 05:24.491
Was it really necessary to go that far?

05:25.158 --> 05:26.117
What?

05:26.201 --> 05:30.247
I don't think we had to go so far
as to erase Woo-seok's memory.

05:30.831 --> 05:33.458
We could've just explained it
and sent him on his way.

05:34.125 --> 05:36.253
You still don't seem
to grasp the situation.

05:36.336 --> 05:38.630
If you'd talked to him nicely
and sent him on his way,

05:38.713 --> 05:41.049
do you think
you'd ever sleep soundly again?

05:41.591 --> 05:42.551
What do you mean?

05:42.634 --> 05:44.928
Well, let me give you an example.

05:45.762 --> 05:49.307
If you just dropped dead tonight,

05:49.391 --> 05:51.101
who do you think would benefit?

05:51.184 --> 05:52.185
What?

05:52.269 --> 05:54.437
No more worrying about
when he'd have to switch back

05:54.521 --> 05:57.941
or about ending up back
in this shabby rooftop place.

05:58.024 --> 06:01.152
Everything he has now
would be his forever.

06:02.070 --> 06:05.031
How long do you think
it'll take him to realize that?

06:05.574 --> 06:06.658
A day or two?

06:06.741 --> 06:10.745
Jeez, why is your example so morbid?

06:10.829 --> 06:14.040
What, are you saying Woo-seok
will try to kill me or something?

06:14.124 --> 06:16.251
Come on, that's nonsense.

06:16.334 --> 06:17.419
Don't you remember?

06:17.502 --> 06:19.796
What did your friend do
when I gave him the chance

06:19.880 --> 06:21.631
to switch your lives back?

06:21.715 --> 06:23.383
I mean, that was then.

06:24.009 --> 06:26.094
This is a different situation.

06:26.177 --> 06:28.722
Besides, Woo-seok's not that kind of guy.

06:28.805 --> 06:30.849
Get real. Humans are all the same.

06:30.932 --> 06:33.560
You think there's
a special "kind" that's any different?

06:34.853 --> 06:37.230
Anyway, erasing his memory
is just a temporary fix.

06:37.314 --> 06:40.984
An eight-tailed fox doesn't have the power
to fully wipe a human's memory.

06:41.985 --> 06:44.821
Whether it takes a few days
or a few months,

06:44.905 --> 06:47.991
your friend's memory will eventually
come back, bit by bit.

06:48.074 --> 06:50.160
Oh, really?

06:50.243 --> 06:52.954
So we need to get back to how things were

06:53.038 --> 06:55.707
before your friend remembers
and gets any funny ideas.

06:56.833 --> 06:59.586
Now that the nuisance is taken care of,

06:59.669 --> 07:02.213
why don't you finish what you were saying?

07:02.297 --> 07:03.506
You found a way?

07:04.257 --> 07:05.592
Right, yes.

07:05.675 --> 07:06.718
All we need is

07:07.677 --> 07:10.513
for you and me to switch fates.

07:11.056 --> 07:12.682
Like you did with him.

07:20.941 --> 07:22.400
What?

07:37.540 --> 07:38.917
What's with her?

07:47.342 --> 07:50.136
EPISODE 6
THE FALSE KINDNESS

08:03.984 --> 08:05.151
Come in.

08:09.072 --> 08:11.116
PERSONAL PROFILE
KANG SI-YEOL

08:11.199 --> 08:12.784
So who is this guy?

08:12.867 --> 08:13.910
Nobody special.

08:14.536 --> 08:17.247
He went through rehab for about a year
after the accident,

08:17.330 --> 08:19.582
and his soccer career
went downhill after that.

08:20.208 --> 08:22.961
He was recently cut
from a fourth division team too.

08:23.044 --> 08:24.421
So what does he do now?

08:25.422 --> 08:27.048
He doesn't seem to have a job.

08:28.675 --> 08:30.176
So, does he come from a rich family?

08:30.260 --> 08:31.636
Not at all.

08:32.137 --> 08:35.849
He has no parents
and no inheritance either.

08:37.726 --> 08:39.060
That can't be right.

08:39.936 --> 08:43.648
He's a client of that money-grubbing fox,
and you're telling me he's broke?

08:45.025 --> 08:46.776
That makes no sense.

08:47.569 --> 08:48.653
Anything else peculiar?

08:49.779 --> 08:52.907
There's something I found out
during the investigation.

08:52.991 --> 08:55.577
You know the boy
who was a witness to that incident?

08:55.660 --> 08:57.829
Apparently, he's Hyeon Woo-seok.

08:58.496 --> 08:59.748
Hyeon Woo-seok?

08:59.831 --> 09:01.041
While you were away,

09:01.124 --> 09:03.418
this athlete named Hyeon Woo-seok
became a huge star--

09:03.501 --> 09:06.087
I watched the World Cup in prison too.

09:06.171 --> 09:07.130
I know who he is.

09:07.213 --> 09:08.882
Oh, okay.

09:11.551 --> 09:13.344
Hyeon Woo-seok.

09:16.264 --> 09:19.517
Kang Si-yeol is completely broke,

09:20.143 --> 09:22.062
but Hyeon Woo-seok is his friend?

09:27.067 --> 09:30.945
I think I should meet this Hyeon Woo-seok.

09:45.877 --> 09:47.879
I feel a bit better now.

09:47.962 --> 09:50.423
Usually, I last half a day in human form,

09:51.049 --> 09:53.259
but erasing his memory
must have drained me.

09:53.343 --> 09:56.179
If you've got your strength back,

09:56.262 --> 09:58.223
could you finish
what you were saying earlier?

09:58.306 --> 10:00.225
Earlier? I meant exactly what I said.

10:00.892 --> 10:04.896
I mean, is switching fates
actually possible for you?

10:04.979 --> 10:07.649
You tried switching Woo-seok
and me back last night,

10:07.732 --> 10:09.025
but it didn't work.

10:09.526 --> 10:13.822
That's because I lack power right now,
but what if I become a nine-tailed fox?

10:16.574 --> 10:17.575
What?

10:17.659 --> 10:20.328
Then I'll have powers too,

10:20.411 --> 10:22.247
so we can just switch our fates.

10:22.330 --> 10:24.791
You can become
a nine-tailed fox instead of me,

10:24.874 --> 10:26.793
and I can become human faster.

10:26.876 --> 10:28.002
It's good for both of us.

10:29.337 --> 10:30.797
Then what about me?

10:30.880 --> 10:33.049
I don't think
there's anything I can do about that.

10:33.133 --> 10:35.969
But she can probably help you later.

10:36.052 --> 10:37.470
Wait, why?

10:37.554 --> 10:40.431
You could just switch me back first
after you become a nine-tailed fox.

10:40.515 --> 10:41.724
It's urgent for me too.

10:41.808 --> 10:43.268
It doesn't work that way

10:43.351 --> 10:45.353
because I'm the one who cast that spell.

10:46.354 --> 10:47.897
- But--
- I'm younger than her,

10:47.981 --> 10:50.483
and my spiritual power is much weaker.

10:50.567 --> 10:54.529
So even if I become a nine-tailed fox,
it'd be hard for me to undo her spell.

10:55.738 --> 10:58.116
Well, okay then.

10:58.199 --> 11:01.953
It doesn't matter how we get there
as long as I get my life back.

11:02.579 --> 11:03.997
Well, the logic holds up.

11:04.956 --> 11:06.207
So problem solved, right?

11:10.003 --> 11:11.504
Nothing's solved.

11:12.672 --> 11:15.258
I was wondering
what you were talking about.

11:16.259 --> 11:19.220
That doesn't sound like your idea, though.

11:20.263 --> 11:22.098
Who told you that crap?

11:23.183 --> 11:24.184
Pardon?

11:25.185 --> 11:27.103
Well…

11:27.187 --> 11:30.398
I was told not to say anything
because it's a secret.

11:30.982 --> 11:32.817
You don't have to say it. It's obvious.

11:33.443 --> 11:34.944
What's obvious?

11:35.028 --> 11:37.155
Just go. Quit talking nonsense.

11:37.655 --> 11:39.532
- But sis--
- I said, go.

11:39.616 --> 11:41.451
You're talking nonsense.

11:41.534 --> 11:45.038
Why are you chasing her off?

11:45.830 --> 11:47.916
- Should I really go?
- No.

11:47.999 --> 11:49.209
Listen to me.

11:49.292 --> 11:52.837
I'm telling you this
for your own good, so pay attention.

11:53.379 --> 11:57.050
You are being scammed.

11:59.177 --> 12:00.094
What?

12:00.762 --> 12:02.263
Why do you want to become human?

12:02.347 --> 12:03.681
What do you know about them?

12:03.765 --> 12:07.101
Do you honestly think
that was your own idea and decision?

12:07.977 --> 12:08.978
Well…

12:09.729 --> 12:11.439
Isn't that just the way it works?

12:11.522 --> 12:14.150
It's what all the other foxes did.

12:14.234 --> 12:16.402
And the ones above said
it's the right path.

12:16.486 --> 12:19.197
Works for me.
If I trick a clueless kid like you,

12:19.280 --> 12:21.407
I can become a nine-tailed fox again.

12:21.491 --> 12:22.408
But what about you?

12:23.034 --> 12:24.953
You turn human, totally unprepared.

12:25.036 --> 12:26.204
Then what?

12:27.038 --> 12:28.456
When you regret it later,

12:28.539 --> 12:32.126
you think the ones above
are going to help you?

12:39.050 --> 12:42.262
What's so bad about living as a human?

12:42.345 --> 12:44.514
I like it. I'm satisfied.

12:44.597 --> 12:46.724
You're satisfied? Right now?

12:46.808 --> 12:49.102
Hey, that's different.

12:49.185 --> 12:51.646
I'm only in this mess because of you.

12:51.729 --> 12:53.606
I was perfectly happy with my old life.

12:53.690 --> 12:55.108
It's all the same.

12:55.191 --> 12:57.443
You could've fallen apart
at any time, with or without me.

12:57.527 --> 12:58.861
Isn't that what human life is?

12:59.696 --> 13:01.698
You never know
how your life will turn out either.

13:01.781 --> 13:03.491
Your old age might be miserable.

13:03.574 --> 13:04.575
What?

13:04.659 --> 13:06.244
Did you seriously just say that to me?

13:06.327 --> 13:08.830
Anyway, I'll figure out
how to change back on my own.

13:08.913 --> 13:11.791
So go live your own life
and mind your own business.

13:12.458 --> 13:13.543
But…

13:13.626 --> 13:16.254
No, no. You don't get to
decide that for her.

13:16.337 --> 13:19.090
She just wants to become human
as soon as possible.

13:19.173 --> 13:20.133
Unlike you.

13:20.216 --> 13:23.052
She didn't make that decision
knowing all the facts.

13:24.137 --> 13:26.848
You'll be glad you stayed
a nine-tailed fox in the end.

13:26.931 --> 13:29.892
But like I said, that's not your call.

13:29.976 --> 13:32.645
How is what you're doing any different
from the ones above?

13:33.479 --> 13:34.480
What?

13:34.564 --> 13:37.608
You chose your own way of life, right?

13:37.692 --> 13:40.153
Well, she's got her own path too.

13:40.236 --> 13:41.195
Right?

13:41.279 --> 13:43.823
I mean, I guess.

13:43.906 --> 13:45.867
What do you mean by that?

13:45.950 --> 13:48.828
So you're dead set on becoming human?

13:50.163 --> 13:51.497
Well…

13:52.415 --> 13:55.126
The decision's up to you.
Don't worry about anyone else.

13:56.044 --> 13:57.962
You want to become human, don't you?

13:58.046 --> 14:00.298
That's right!
You decide since it's your life.

14:08.014 --> 14:11.601
Now that you're both pressuring me,
I'm not so sure.

14:15.480 --> 14:17.940
Talking to you is pointless.

14:21.486 --> 14:22.737
VIOLENT CRIMES UNIT 2

14:22.820 --> 14:26.115
Let go of me! I'm the victim here!

14:26.199 --> 14:28.117
You're going to pay for this!

14:28.201 --> 14:30.119
Get your hands off me!

14:35.583 --> 14:37.668
I'm scared, sis.

14:38.252 --> 14:39.921
Don't look away. Watch.

14:40.755 --> 14:41.881
If you become human,

14:41.964 --> 14:44.217
you'll have to live among trash like them.

14:44.300 --> 14:45.718
What?

14:45.802 --> 14:47.261
I have to live around them?

14:47.929 --> 14:48.971
With people like that?

14:49.055 --> 14:52.767
She won't run
into people like them very often.

14:52.850 --> 14:54.060
Yes, she will.

14:55.269 --> 14:59.232
These people can spot
clueless kids like you

14:59.315 --> 15:01.692
a mile away, you know?

15:01.776 --> 15:03.194
Just look at her face.

15:03.277 --> 15:05.029
Doesn't it just scream "easy target"?

15:13.454 --> 15:15.832
Hey, what are you in for?

15:17.208 --> 15:19.377
- Mugging.
- You?

15:19.460 --> 15:21.587
- Online scam.
- You?

15:21.671 --> 15:23.256
- Assault.
- You?

15:23.339 --> 15:24.590
Illegal filming on the subway.

15:25.967 --> 15:28.469
Wow, you must be so proud of yourselves!

15:28.553 --> 15:29.762
Excuse me.

15:30.471 --> 15:32.515
- Who are you?
- Never mind.

15:32.598 --> 15:34.725
Make sure you investigate them thoroughly.

15:36.144 --> 15:37.395
See that?

15:37.478 --> 15:40.189
The human world will rob you blind
right under your nose.

15:40.273 --> 15:42.608
Do you really think

15:42.692 --> 15:46.404
you can survive
dropping into this den of evil?

15:47.405 --> 15:48.489
Well…

15:48.573 --> 15:49.907
Hey, hold on.

15:49.991 --> 15:53.286
You shouldn't pressure her
for an answer in a place like this.

15:55.997 --> 15:59.792
The human world has its good side too.

15:59.876 --> 16:02.753
This time, I'll take you somewhere nice.

16:09.218 --> 16:13.055
Feel free to eat whatever you want here
without worrying about what others think.

16:13.764 --> 16:15.016
Really?

16:15.099 --> 16:17.643
In all my 500 years,
I've never seen so much food.

16:20.646 --> 16:22.315
Wait, hold on.

16:23.941 --> 16:24.901
Like this.

16:40.500 --> 16:43.169
Slow down.
No one's going to take it from you.

16:46.047 --> 16:49.217
This is the best food
I've had in half a century.

16:49.300 --> 16:51.302
That's because you were stuck
in the mountains,

16:51.385 --> 16:54.472
eating nothing but greens.

16:54.555 --> 16:57.308
This is nothing, really.

16:59.101 --> 17:01.103
Back when I was a nine-tailed fox,

17:02.021 --> 17:04.732
I ate way better stuff than this.

17:05.441 --> 17:08.486
There are so many delicious things
in the human world.

17:08.569 --> 17:11.781
If you become human,
you can eat like this every day.

17:18.829 --> 17:20.498
You really think so?

17:22.833 --> 17:26.295
You can't just go in there.

17:29.048 --> 17:31.592
How much do you think
that meal you ate cost?

17:33.678 --> 17:35.054
I don't know.

17:35.137 --> 17:36.597
The human world has classes.

17:36.681 --> 17:38.057
Here…

17:40.268 --> 17:41.477
Right.

17:41.561 --> 17:43.479
That one over there is at the very bottom.

17:43.563 --> 17:47.316
No matter how many dishes she washes,

17:47.400 --> 17:49.652
she'll never be able
to afford a meal like you just ate.

17:49.735 --> 17:52.405
Why? Because the pay is garbage.

17:52.947 --> 17:55.116
Who starts out as a chef from day one?

17:55.199 --> 17:56.742
Everyone works their way up.

17:56.826 --> 18:00.580
You think hard work is
all it takes to get to the top?

18:00.663 --> 18:05.585
There are tons of humans who end up
washing dishes their whole lives.

18:13.384 --> 18:14.552
You have to leave!

18:14.635 --> 18:16.512
Just get out, please.

18:16.596 --> 18:18.097
Unbelievable.

18:18.180 --> 18:19.432
I'm sorry.

18:20.433 --> 18:22.643
You got us kicked out
before we could really eat.

18:22.727 --> 18:25.646
- Did I say anything wrong?
- Wrong or not, that's not the point.

18:25.730 --> 18:27.607
Why on earth are you taking it this far?

18:30.192 --> 18:33.029
Do you actually have another way
to get back to how it was?

18:33.863 --> 18:35.031
Well…

18:37.199 --> 18:38.326
Not right now, but--

18:38.409 --> 18:41.912
See? You don't have one.
This is the only way.

18:41.996 --> 18:44.498
So why are you being so difficult?

18:46.292 --> 18:47.960
I'm not.

18:48.044 --> 18:52.048
But you're saying I should just stand by
and watch when I know how this turns out?

18:52.131 --> 18:55.259
It's obvious what'll happen
if that idiot suddenly becomes human.

18:55.343 --> 18:57.970
Since when did you care so much
about other people?

18:58.054 --> 18:59.472
What?

19:01.265 --> 19:03.517
Excuse me.

19:04.435 --> 19:07.813
We went to the police station
because you wanted to,

19:07.897 --> 19:11.275
and we came to this restaurant
because Si-yeol wanted to.

19:13.694 --> 19:14.820
So?

19:15.780 --> 19:19.950
So, isn't it my turn to go where I want?

19:20.785 --> 19:24.080
There's somewhere I've always
wanted to go in the human world.

19:32.713 --> 19:33.964
Sis!

19:34.674 --> 19:36.550
She doesn't know the first thing
about the world,

19:36.634 --> 19:38.719
so where did she even hear
about a place like this?

19:38.803 --> 19:42.556
She said the stranded kid she saved
kept bragging about it.

19:43.265 --> 19:44.850
Just play along.

19:48.646 --> 19:50.856
What's so fun about that anyway?

19:51.524 --> 19:54.193
Si-yeol, how long do we have to do this?

20:01.575 --> 20:04.412
Now, that's better.

20:14.547 --> 20:16.173
- Did you have fun?
- Yes!

20:18.509 --> 20:21.345
But the kids in front of me and behind me

20:21.429 --> 20:23.347
were all riding with their mom or dad.

20:23.431 --> 20:24.515
So?

20:24.598 --> 20:27.268
You want me to act like your mom now?

20:27.893 --> 20:30.312
No, it's just that I keep riding alone.

20:30.396 --> 20:33.524
You should be grateful
we even came here with you.

20:33.607 --> 20:34.942
No!

20:47.496 --> 20:49.957
Tell them to stop this thing!

21:08.267 --> 21:09.643
That was so much fun, sis!

21:09.727 --> 21:11.103
Let's ride it again!

21:11.187 --> 21:12.521
I can't ride it again.

21:12.605 --> 21:14.648
Why not?

21:15.608 --> 21:19.695
This is a really popular ride,
so the line takes forever.

21:19.779 --> 21:22.239
Is that why?

21:24.867 --> 21:26.202
What's going on?

21:26.285 --> 21:28.329
This fixes everything, right?
We don't have to wait.

21:28.412 --> 21:29.789
No, don't!

21:29.872 --> 21:31.248
Don't do it!

21:33.667 --> 21:34.543
What the…

21:35.961 --> 21:38.297
I'm going to kill that idiot fox!

21:55.731 --> 21:57.358
Hey, are you okay?

21:58.442 --> 22:01.237
I'm dizzy, and I feel sick.

22:02.029 --> 22:03.364
I feel like I'm dying.

22:04.156 --> 22:06.325
This damn human body.

22:08.118 --> 22:09.829
I'm so sorry, sis.

22:10.538 --> 22:12.456
I thought you'd like it too.

22:13.499 --> 22:14.416
Hey.

22:14.500 --> 22:17.169
Look at me right now.
Doesn't it make you feel anything?

22:17.253 --> 22:18.546
Do you still want to be--

22:19.713 --> 22:21.423
Sis, let's go on that one next!

22:25.177 --> 22:27.221
Is a tail really
the only thing she's missing?

22:27.304 --> 22:28.472
If you ask me,

22:28.556 --> 22:31.183
I think she's got you
wrapped around her finger.

22:32.142 --> 22:33.227
What?

22:34.770 --> 22:37.481
Just accept it. It's easier that way.

22:38.774 --> 22:40.359
We're coming.

23:21.942 --> 23:23.193
That hurts.

23:23.277 --> 23:25.362
It really hurts!

23:26.030 --> 23:28.157
You of all people
shouldn't be scared of that!

23:30.576 --> 23:34.163
I wasn't scared. I was just startled.

23:35.039 --> 23:37.333
Those fake ghosts aren't even scary.

23:40.502 --> 23:41.503
Unbelievable.

24:02.399 --> 24:06.654
The Divine Spirit told me
that an ominous guest would arrive today.

24:10.824 --> 24:12.451
That must be you.

24:14.662 --> 24:18.040
They say you're
the best shaman in Sancheong.

24:20.209 --> 24:23.212
You've invited quite the ghost in.

24:27.466 --> 24:32.638
The sorrow of losing one's family
is a pain anyone can sympathize with.

24:33.180 --> 24:37.685
But you dare defy the will of Heaven
and devour every divine spirit?

24:37.768 --> 24:39.812
Save your breath.

24:39.895 --> 24:44.358
I have my reasons,
so hand over that ghost behind you.

24:49.071 --> 24:53.450
I was trying to catch a fox,
but it was just too vicious.

24:53.534 --> 24:55.411
I'm running low on spiritual energy.

24:56.036 --> 24:58.956
The karma you carry
is already as deep as the ocean.

24:59.039 --> 25:01.083
How will you handle all that sin?

25:01.834 --> 25:05.921
What's a little rain to the ocean?

25:07.131 --> 25:08.215
So,

25:09.883 --> 25:11.802
let's not be too difficult about this.

26:02.936 --> 26:06.356
I never thought I'd say this,

26:07.066 --> 26:09.068
but even after things go back to normal,

26:09.651 --> 26:12.404
I'll probably still think about today
from time to time.

26:15.991 --> 26:17.201
I mean,

26:17.826 --> 26:19.995
it's my first time at a place like this.

26:22.331 --> 26:24.458
You've never been to an amusement park?

26:25.250 --> 26:28.045
Don't humans go to these places
all the time as kids?

26:28.796 --> 26:30.547
My grandmother was out working,

26:30.631 --> 26:33.008
so I never got to visit places
like this as a kid.

26:33.092 --> 26:36.929
And being on the sports team,
I hardly ever got to go on field trips.

26:38.680 --> 26:41.934
You haven't really done much, have you?

26:42.017 --> 26:43.227
I've been everywhere.

26:43.310 --> 26:45.771
Jayeon Nongwon, Bugok Hawaii, you name it.

26:46.730 --> 26:48.148
You have?

26:48.232 --> 26:50.067
You were just puking your guts out.

26:50.692 --> 26:52.945
That's because of this damn human body.

26:53.028 --> 26:56.740
You get sick from just a few rides

26:56.824 --> 26:58.867
and have to wait an hour
for a one-minute ride.

26:58.951 --> 27:01.870
How is this supposed to be fun?

27:01.954 --> 27:03.330
You know,

27:03.413 --> 27:06.959
you look like
you're having the most fun here.

27:11.755 --> 27:12.840
I only did this

27:14.591 --> 27:16.635
because you guys made me.

27:26.228 --> 27:27.312
What's wrong?

27:28.272 --> 27:30.107
- What?
- Let me see.

27:33.235 --> 27:35.445
Your heel is all scraped up.

27:35.529 --> 27:38.031
Why didn't you tell me
before it got this bad?

27:39.116 --> 27:41.827
I thought this was normal
when you walk a lot.

27:43.036 --> 27:44.329
That's ridiculous.

27:45.789 --> 27:47.374
Jeez, you're bleeding.

27:47.457 --> 27:48.792
That must've really hurt.

27:54.965 --> 27:55.924
Wait.

27:57.009 --> 28:00.179
Are you worried about me right now?

28:01.346 --> 28:02.264
Why?

28:02.764 --> 28:04.933
Am I not allowed to worry about you?

28:09.771 --> 28:10.856
I mean,

28:11.481 --> 28:14.151
it's just unexpected, that's all.

28:15.986 --> 28:18.155
Technically, what you're suffering through

28:19.198 --> 28:23.994
is also kind of my fault, in a way.

28:24.620 --> 28:25.621
So…

28:26.121 --> 28:28.373
So, is it your fault or not?

28:30.083 --> 28:31.710
I don't know. Think whatever you want.

28:33.086 --> 28:34.671
It just so happens that right now,

28:34.755 --> 28:37.883
you're the only person
in the world on my side.

28:38.592 --> 28:41.803
I don't have any friends or family
I can rely on.

28:42.554 --> 28:45.057
You're all I have.

28:45.682 --> 28:48.352
So you should worry about me too.

28:48.435 --> 28:50.145
I'll be worrying about you.

28:55.901 --> 29:00.322
And if anything were to happen to you,
I'd never be able to go back to my life.

29:00.405 --> 29:02.241
So how can I not worry?

29:02.824 --> 29:05.953
Especially with all the enemies
you've made with your misdeeds.

29:08.080 --> 29:09.289
What?

29:09.831 --> 29:12.042
Now that sounds more like you.

29:12.125 --> 29:13.710
Anyway, just wait here.

29:13.794 --> 29:15.337
I'll go grab a bandage.

29:24.638 --> 29:25.806
Sis!

29:35.774 --> 29:37.276
So, what's your wish?

29:37.901 --> 29:38.944
What?

29:39.027 --> 29:42.614
We made a bet
about a hundred years ago, remember?

29:42.698 --> 29:45.367
We said that whoever becomes human first
gets their wish granted.

29:45.450 --> 29:46.743
Don't tell me you forgot.

29:47.369 --> 29:49.162
Oh, that?

29:50.289 --> 29:53.500
Do you want me to dig up
that wild ginseng I hid?

29:53.583 --> 29:56.253
I hear it sells for a fortune
in the human world.

29:56.795 --> 29:58.922
Or maybe I should visit
the king in his dreams

29:59.006 --> 30:02.968
to tell him to promote that scholar
you've got a crush on.

30:03.635 --> 30:05.971
The mountain god
will scold you for that.

30:06.054 --> 30:08.348
Only if I get caught.

30:08.432 --> 30:11.059
You think I'm like you?

30:11.143 --> 30:12.853
I know how to get around the rules.

30:12.936 --> 30:16.148
I don't want to wish for things like that.
My wish is…

30:21.862 --> 30:25.824
for you to do good deeds
and focus on your cultivation.

30:27.034 --> 30:29.703
What? I do that every single day.

30:32.581 --> 30:34.082
Not things like that--

30:34.166 --> 30:37.627
So that you become human quickly.

30:38.462 --> 30:40.672
We could live in the same village,

30:40.756 --> 30:45.719
make mugwort rice cakes in the spring,
and make kimchi in the winter.

30:46.928 --> 30:50.223
Wouldn't it be nice
to grow old together like that?

30:55.520 --> 30:57.647
But Geum-ho…

30:58.315 --> 30:59.316
Yes?

31:00.942 --> 31:03.278
What if it takes me a long time?

31:05.864 --> 31:09.785
What if I finally become human,
and you're already a hunchbacked granny?

31:09.868 --> 31:11.578
Hey, don't say that.

31:13.372 --> 31:16.541
Grandma! Let's go pick mugwort!

31:16.625 --> 31:17.709
Grandma!

31:19.211 --> 31:20.754
- Let go of me!
- No!

31:20.837 --> 31:22.047
Let go!

31:22.714 --> 31:23.924
Never!

31:25.592 --> 31:27.219
Sis!

31:29.638 --> 31:31.264
Why are you standing here alone?

31:33.642 --> 31:34.684
Tell me.

31:35.310 --> 31:37.646
Do you still want to become
human that badly?

31:39.272 --> 31:40.148
What?

31:40.232 --> 31:43.235
I used to know someone a long time ago.

31:44.319 --> 31:46.488
She was a fox, just like us.

31:47.114 --> 31:51.201
She cultivated herself for a long time
and finally became human.

31:52.911 --> 31:54.538
What happened to her?

31:55.956 --> 31:57.249
She died

31:57.916 --> 32:01.461
after dragging herself through a long,
cruel, miserable life.

32:03.922 --> 32:06.508
That's what human life is to me.

32:07.092 --> 32:09.803
It's fleeting, weak, and fragile.

32:11.263 --> 32:15.058
And you still want to be one of them?

32:22.274 --> 32:23.442
You know,

32:24.776 --> 32:26.361
today was really special for me.

32:27.195 --> 32:28.488
How about for you?

32:30.449 --> 32:31.450
What?

32:31.533 --> 32:34.453
All this time, I wasn't exactly happy,

32:34.536 --> 32:36.913
but I wasn't exactly unhappy either.

32:37.664 --> 32:39.708
I just haven't had any days
that were memorable.

32:39.791 --> 32:42.085
That's because you've been holed up
in the mountains--

32:42.169 --> 32:43.879
Then what about you?

32:44.504 --> 32:46.840
You've lived in the human world
this whole time.

32:46.923 --> 32:49.134
Have you had a lot of happy days?

32:50.469 --> 32:52.762
Or even terribly unhappy ones?

32:56.600 --> 32:58.143
I want to become human.

32:58.226 --> 33:00.353
Maybe I'll be unhappy.

33:00.437 --> 33:03.190
Maybe there will be moments
I can barely stand.

33:03.273 --> 33:04.483
But still,

33:04.566 --> 33:06.985
I want to live a life that's memorable.

33:07.944 --> 33:10.447
Even if it's short,
I want it to be intense.

33:12.157 --> 33:13.700
I want to be swept away.

33:14.242 --> 33:19.873
Not a life where I can predict
and control everything.

33:19.956 --> 33:22.959
I want to be tossed about, swept along,

33:23.585 --> 33:25.629
crying one minute, laughing the next.

33:25.712 --> 33:27.672
I want to live a real life.

33:29.633 --> 33:33.220
Some days,
I want to be torn apart by regret.

33:33.887 --> 33:35.472
I want to feel hollow.

33:35.555 --> 33:39.559
But when I laugh,
I want to laugh out loud.

33:42.312 --> 33:43.271
Sis.

33:44.356 --> 33:48.360
Even if I'm unhappy, sad,

33:49.194 --> 33:50.946
and eventually die,

33:51.613 --> 33:53.156
I still want to become human.

33:56.159 --> 33:58.119
I will never become human.

33:59.371 --> 34:02.082
I won't love a human as you did.

34:02.707 --> 34:05.168
I won't live in misery,
and I won't die in despair.

34:05.961 --> 34:07.337
I'll never

34:08.588 --> 34:10.507
live like you.

34:14.553 --> 34:15.679
Eun-ho.

34:19.766 --> 34:21.017
Geum-ho?

34:22.060 --> 34:23.270
Are you with me?

34:25.272 --> 34:26.606
Do you recognize me?

34:28.233 --> 34:29.234
I've…

34:30.360 --> 34:32.571
lived my own life

34:33.530 --> 34:35.031
with no regrets.

34:35.824 --> 34:39.160
You need to live yours.

34:40.412 --> 34:43.915
Whatever that may be.

34:59.973 --> 35:01.558
Yeon-su?

35:03.143 --> 35:04.686
Isn't that Yeon-su over there?

35:05.979 --> 35:07.355
No way.

35:07.439 --> 35:10.317
She's single. How could she have two kids?

35:13.737 --> 35:15.864
Goodness, these kids.

35:16.489 --> 35:18.408
They've made a mess here too.

35:31.796 --> 35:33.840
Mom, hurry up!

35:33.923 --> 35:35.634
Yeah, I'm coming!

35:44.893 --> 35:46.728
Why are you being so moody?

35:48.438 --> 35:49.522
Hold this.

35:53.777 --> 35:55.528
You are so stubborn.

35:55.612 --> 35:59.032
You're not a nine-tailed fox
who can use earth-folding anymore.

36:07.040 --> 36:08.708
Where did the other one go, anyway?

36:09.626 --> 36:10.502
She left.

36:11.294 --> 36:13.129
What? Where to?

36:13.213 --> 36:14.297
Where do you think?

36:14.381 --> 36:16.508
She's from the mountains,
so she went back.

36:16.591 --> 36:18.343
- Let's go.
- Wait, hold on.

36:18.426 --> 36:20.553
Wait for me.

36:20.637 --> 36:21.721
Hey!

36:22.472 --> 36:24.057
What's going on?

36:24.557 --> 36:26.518
Did you guys fight while I was gone?

36:27.435 --> 36:28.687
If that's not it--

36:28.770 --> 36:30.647
You got exactly what you wanted.

36:30.730 --> 36:32.482
- What?
- We didn't fight.

36:32.565 --> 36:34.651
We decided to switch our fates.

36:34.734 --> 36:36.194
- Really?
- Yes.

36:36.277 --> 36:37.570
Wait, hold on.

36:38.196 --> 36:39.197
For real?

36:39.698 --> 36:42.033
So it's all sorted?
Do I get my life back now?

36:44.160 --> 36:46.162
Get a grip, Si-yeol.

36:46.246 --> 36:49.207
You can't just
go back to normal overnight.

36:50.500 --> 36:52.043
Why not?

36:52.127 --> 36:54.671
Did you already forget the condition?

36:55.296 --> 36:58.717
That half-wit eight-tailed fox
has to become a nine-tailed fox

36:58.800 --> 37:00.760
before we can change our fates.

37:01.553 --> 37:02.554
Right.

37:03.972 --> 37:06.141
But how long will that take?

37:06.224 --> 37:07.642
Will it be quick?

37:07.726 --> 37:09.894
Usually, it takes about 100 years.

37:11.062 --> 37:13.064
What? A hundred years?

37:13.148 --> 37:15.567
Did you think
growing an additional tail was easy?

37:15.650 --> 37:18.361
How can you be so calm about this?

37:18.445 --> 37:20.613
You think you'll still be alive by then?

37:20.697 --> 37:24.492
Oh, come on! What's the point
if I die of old age first?

37:24.576 --> 37:26.745
I said, usually.

37:29.122 --> 37:31.291
So there's another way?

37:32.125 --> 37:35.211
It takes 100 years for total rookies.

37:35.295 --> 37:37.088
But I'm a pro.

37:37.714 --> 37:40.008
I've got some tricks up my sleeve.

37:46.639 --> 37:47.766
Is that…

37:49.350 --> 37:50.643
Brace yourself.

37:50.727 --> 37:53.772
Just so you know, this won't be easy.

37:54.314 --> 37:57.192
We'll be slammed starting tomorrow.

38:18.087 --> 38:19.088
What?

38:19.172 --> 38:21.549
I was too distracted to notice before,

38:21.633 --> 38:24.552
but this place is a total dump.

38:26.346 --> 38:27.430
What?

38:28.014 --> 38:31.100
You call this a home?

38:31.184 --> 38:33.770
You can be broke and still have taste.

38:33.853 --> 38:35.730
A roof and walls don't make a home.

38:35.814 --> 38:37.357
Are you kidding me?

38:37.982 --> 38:39.734
This isn't even really my place.

38:40.693 --> 38:43.947
I changed your fate,
not your sense of style.

38:44.030 --> 38:46.282
You just don't remember it,

38:46.366 --> 38:49.452
but you're the one
who decorated this place.

38:50.036 --> 38:51.913
And I saw your original place too.

38:51.996 --> 38:54.249
It was completely empty.

38:54.332 --> 38:56.709
Just some weird machine
you get into naked.

38:57.335 --> 39:01.923
That's just a crash pad
for when I'm in Korea.

39:03.091 --> 39:07.637
My actual house in the UK
has a pool and a private theater.

39:07.720 --> 39:10.473
The closet is huge, and the decor is--

39:10.557 --> 39:13.268
This is so depressing.

39:13.768 --> 39:18.106
I need to change back as soon as possible.
I can't live like this.

39:18.731 --> 39:21.484
Yeah, I'm rooting for you.

39:23.570 --> 39:24.904
Where are you going?

39:24.988 --> 39:25.905
What?

39:25.989 --> 39:28.199
Why? You need something?

39:28.700 --> 39:30.577
I'm tired. I'm going to go rest.

39:30.660 --> 39:34.122
I get that you're tired,
but why are you going in there?

39:34.205 --> 39:36.916
There's only one bedroom,
so obviously it's mine.

39:37.000 --> 39:40.545
This is my home.
And I slept in there last night, didn't I?

39:40.628 --> 39:43.423
That's because I slept
with the eight-tailed fox.

39:43.506 --> 39:45.884
Starting today, I get the bed.

39:46.426 --> 39:47.886
I'm the oldest here.

39:49.387 --> 39:52.098
Sure, whatever you say.

39:52.181 --> 39:55.768
You're older than the Republic of Korea.
How can I beat that?

39:55.852 --> 39:57.562
I'll just have to serve you.

40:02.358 --> 40:04.068
Then I'm going to go wash up.

40:05.737 --> 40:06.946
Hold it.

40:07.030 --> 40:08.948
I get to shower first too.

40:09.032 --> 40:10.783
Elders first.

40:47.195 --> 40:48.154
Si-yeol.

40:50.615 --> 40:51.616
Si-yeol.

40:52.784 --> 40:53.993
Wake up.

40:55.578 --> 40:56.663
Hello?

40:59.874 --> 41:01.084
My gosh!

41:01.626 --> 41:03.586
What do you want now?

41:04.379 --> 41:05.797
I'm hungry.

41:05.880 --> 41:07.799
What? At this hour?

41:09.008 --> 41:10.426
Come on.

41:10.510 --> 41:12.553
You said you were stuffed
from the lunch buffet.

41:12.637 --> 41:13.888
So you refused to eat dinner.

41:13.972 --> 41:15.848
I was full then.

41:16.474 --> 41:18.810
Now I'm hungry, so I can't sleep.

41:18.893 --> 41:21.396
This damn human body.

41:22.313 --> 41:24.107
Just try to go back to sleep.

41:24.190 --> 41:26.401
You'll get fat if you eat this late.

41:27.276 --> 41:31.072
It's fine. Once I turn back,
I won't gain weight anyway.

41:32.782 --> 41:36.077
Any more of that stuff
she was eating yesterday?

41:37.036 --> 41:39.414
What? Ramyeon?

42:00.059 --> 42:01.352
Dig in.

42:11.070 --> 42:12.363
So good.

42:12.447 --> 42:13.823
Is it that good?

42:14.323 --> 42:15.283
Yeah.

42:16.325 --> 42:18.411
Why did you only make one, though?

42:18.494 --> 42:19.537
Aren't you eating?

42:20.204 --> 42:22.165
No, I don't eat at this hour.

42:22.248 --> 42:23.958
Especially not stuff like this.

42:24.959 --> 42:31.090
I think the last time I had ramyeon
was 12 or 13 years ago.

42:33.301 --> 42:34.844
Come on, just have one bite.

42:34.927 --> 42:36.137
It's really good.

42:38.681 --> 42:40.016
No, I'm good.

42:40.641 --> 42:43.561
We both reset when we go back anyway.

42:43.644 --> 42:45.271
Just eat it while you can.

42:49.317 --> 42:51.402
I guess that's true.

42:54.655 --> 42:56.783
Then just one bite.

43:19.097 --> 43:21.349
Come on, surely you want more than that?

43:21.432 --> 43:22.600
What?

43:22.683 --> 43:23.976
Right.

43:24.894 --> 43:26.354
Right?

43:27.230 --> 43:29.398
I'll just have one more bite.

43:40.827 --> 43:42.161
What the heck?

43:48.084 --> 43:48.960
Hey!

43:49.836 --> 43:51.295
You can't just eat it all.

43:51.379 --> 43:53.089
There's nothing left for me!

43:54.882 --> 43:56.259
Should we make another?

43:58.845 --> 43:59.929
Make it two.

44:03.683 --> 44:05.101
Tastes better with three eggs.

44:05.726 --> 44:06.936
- Mix in some rice?
- Yeah.

44:10.690 --> 44:12.150
What is this?

44:12.900 --> 44:13.818
What is it?

44:13.901 --> 44:15.778
What's wrong?

44:16.404 --> 44:19.574
Oh no… my face.

44:22.160 --> 44:24.162
You're all puffy.

44:24.245 --> 44:27.540
I told you not to eat that late.

44:27.623 --> 44:29.667
You think your face looks any better?

44:29.750 --> 44:31.752
You're all puffy too.

44:31.836 --> 44:32.753
Me too?

44:35.006 --> 44:36.966
What the heck?

44:38.718 --> 44:41.470
I think the swelling's going down a bit.

44:41.554 --> 44:43.764
We should've just gone for a run.

44:43.848 --> 44:46.517
I told you we'd be busy starting today.

44:47.185 --> 44:48.811
We can't waste energy on useless stuff.

44:50.855 --> 44:52.398
What an excuse.

44:53.024 --> 44:55.401
Whatever. Just go change the spoons.

44:55.484 --> 44:56.736
Get the cold ones.

44:59.655 --> 45:01.407
- Nice!
- Nice!

45:01.490 --> 45:02.825
That's it!

45:02.909 --> 45:06.370
Move it up! There we go!
Seo Beom, shoot! Shoot it!

45:08.706 --> 45:10.875
- Nice!
- He skied it, damn it.

45:10.958 --> 45:13.502
This is so frustrating.

45:14.128 --> 45:15.880
Coach, would you like some water?

45:15.963 --> 45:17.340
Forget it. Put that away.

45:17.423 --> 45:19.258
- Cross it in!
- Okay!

45:21.219 --> 45:23.429
Come on, block him!

45:25.014 --> 45:27.350
- Block him!
- Block!

45:29.894 --> 45:31.729
Nice!

45:32.271 --> 45:36.025
You've got to move up as a group, okay?

45:36.108 --> 45:37.443
Hey, Bae Jeong-bae!

45:37.526 --> 45:41.405
All you do is send crosses all day.

45:41.489 --> 45:43.366
Try cutting inside sometimes.

45:43.449 --> 45:45.368
And dribble
the ball up the field like this

45:45.451 --> 45:47.203
so that they get confused!

45:47.703 --> 45:48.829
Yes, sir.

45:49.372 --> 45:51.707
How does the water taste,
Seo Beom, you punk?

45:52.291 --> 45:53.459
You call that a shot?

45:53.542 --> 45:54.919
You skied it way up there.

45:55.002 --> 45:56.796
I thought you'd hit a damn airplane.

45:56.879 --> 45:58.005
I'm sorry.

45:58.089 --> 45:59.382
Damn it.

45:59.882 --> 46:03.970
Are you guys just gonna play defense
the whole time and go home?

46:04.053 --> 46:06.681
You have to score goals to win!

46:06.764 --> 46:07.932
But why?

46:08.015 --> 46:10.893
Why isn't anyone making a proper attack?

46:12.144 --> 46:13.312
But, Coach.

46:14.188 --> 46:15.815
Who are we supposed to cut back to?

46:15.898 --> 46:16.899
What?

46:16.983 --> 46:19.652
Well, even if we cut back,
there's nobody there to take it.

46:19.735 --> 46:20.778
Hey, why isn't there?

46:20.861 --> 46:23.155
Kang Si-yeol would be right…

46:28.160 --> 46:30.162
Just pass it to the forward striker.

46:30.871 --> 46:32.581
Who's the forward striker?

46:32.665 --> 46:34.542
- What?
- If we're being realistic,

46:34.625 --> 46:37.670
we don't have a proper striker
on our team right now.

46:44.218 --> 46:48.514
Don't you guys know modern soccer?

46:49.515 --> 46:50.808
Total soccer.

46:50.891 --> 46:53.060
Everyone attacks, everyone defends--

46:53.144 --> 46:54.437
Excuse me, Coach.

46:54.520 --> 46:56.480
- Instead, can't we just--
- No!

46:58.774 --> 47:00.776
You're trying to bring up

47:01.819 --> 47:03.612
Kang Si-yeol again, right?

47:04.822 --> 47:06.449
You listen to me carefully.

47:07.700 --> 47:08.868
Over…

47:10.161 --> 47:12.288
my dead body.

47:13.080 --> 47:14.665
That punk Kang Si-yeol is out!

47:16.542 --> 47:18.002
Out for good!

47:26.510 --> 47:28.888
Didn't you say we'd be super busy?

47:28.971 --> 47:30.556
But we're not exactly fishing here.

47:31.640 --> 47:32.933
What are we doing?

47:35.770 --> 47:37.021
Fishing?

47:37.104 --> 47:38.731
We're doing something similar.

47:38.814 --> 47:40.858
Except we're fishing for people, not fish.

47:41.484 --> 47:43.527
What? Fishing for people?

47:44.236 --> 47:45.279
Yes.

47:45.363 --> 47:48.199
Because from now on,
we're on a "Good Deeds Project."

47:51.035 --> 47:51.994
Fine.

47:52.078 --> 47:55.164
No matter what I say,
I get that you want to become human.

47:55.247 --> 47:56.624
But before that,

47:57.666 --> 48:01.253
becoming a nine-tailed fox
is no easy task to begin with.

48:01.337 --> 48:02.630
Are you ready for that?

48:02.713 --> 48:05.841
Can you follow my lead without complaint,
no matter what I ask?

48:06.884 --> 48:07.927
Follow what exactly?

48:09.887 --> 48:10.930
What?

48:11.013 --> 48:14.183
From here on out, you're on your own.

48:14.266 --> 48:16.185
I'm not the one in a rush.

48:17.061 --> 48:18.145
Wait.

48:19.230 --> 48:20.231
Well…

48:21.065 --> 48:24.777
I mean, I'm still going to help you.

48:25.653 --> 48:29.031
But you need to do good deeds
to build spiritual power so your tails--

48:29.115 --> 48:31.200
Then I'll just give you my fox bead.

48:31.909 --> 48:33.786
I'll use a spell to connect us

48:33.869 --> 48:37.164
so you can do the good deeds
and build the spiritual power for me.

48:41.794 --> 48:44.797
My transformation is about to wear off,
so I have to run.

48:46.257 --> 48:47.508
What do you say?

48:48.300 --> 48:49.927
I think you were right.

48:50.970 --> 48:55.057
I swear, she's got me
wrapped around her finger.

48:56.142 --> 48:59.562
So what you're saying is,
when you do good deeds,

49:00.229 --> 49:03.190
she gains the spiritual power instead?

49:03.274 --> 49:05.526
But you can't actually use
her fox bead's power yourself.

49:05.609 --> 49:06.861
That's right.

49:06.944 --> 49:09.947
That's why from now on,
we have to do good deeds.

49:10.030 --> 49:13.284
Aggressively and in massive amounts
in a short amount of time.

49:15.578 --> 49:19.540
But what does that
have to do with fishing?

49:19.623 --> 49:21.041
Seriously?

49:21.125 --> 49:23.919
Do I have to spell out
every single thing for you?

49:24.003 --> 49:25.337
Who do you think is the reason

49:25.421 --> 49:27.798
I'm stuck as a human
and suffering like this?

49:30.509 --> 49:33.596
It's because I saved your life!

49:35.556 --> 49:38.225
Okay, fine. So what?

49:38.851 --> 49:41.228
One human embodies an entire world,

49:41.312 --> 49:46.734
so saving a person's life
is basically saving an entire world.

49:47.401 --> 49:49.153
In other words,

49:49.236 --> 49:52.948
the ultimate good deed,
the highest virtue of all,

49:53.032 --> 49:54.033
is saving a life.

50:04.710 --> 50:05.711
Wait, don't tell me.

50:06.337 --> 50:08.422
That's not what you're doing, right?

50:08.506 --> 50:11.217
You're waiting for someone to jump
so you can save them?

50:11.842 --> 50:14.178
Why? Is there a problem?

50:14.261 --> 50:15.137
Hey!

50:15.221 --> 50:16.764
Forget the problem!
How's that a good deed?

50:16.847 --> 50:18.432
The karma will get you, you know?

50:19.433 --> 50:22.436
Why would karma get me
when I'm saving a life?

50:24.063 --> 50:25.606
Unbelievable.

50:26.315 --> 50:27.691
Okay, fine.

50:27.775 --> 50:30.945
I don't expect much
from your moral compass anymore,

50:31.028 --> 50:34.490
but putting that aside,
it's just inefficient.

50:34.573 --> 50:36.742
Do you honestly think this makes sense?

50:38.202 --> 50:40.287
- It doesn't?
- No!

50:41.080 --> 50:43.874
It's like lying under a tree
waiting for fruit to fall!

50:43.958 --> 50:45.543
How long do you plan on waiting?

50:45.626 --> 50:46.627
You think so?

50:49.463 --> 50:50.506
I guess you're right.

50:51.173 --> 50:53.968
You do have a point.

50:55.010 --> 50:59.682
Given the urgency,
this does feel too passive.

50:59.765 --> 51:00.766
Exactly.

51:00.849 --> 51:03.102
Even if the good deeds are forced,

51:03.185 --> 51:06.480
we should try to do them the normal way--

51:06.564 --> 51:07.856
Fine.

51:08.399 --> 51:10.442
I'll just have to find another way.

51:16.365 --> 51:18.492
SHAMAN'S SHRINE
ADULT STORE

51:18.576 --> 51:21.120
GAME LAND
IMAGE SHOP

51:25.749 --> 51:27.251
Here, Si-yeol.

51:27.334 --> 51:29.295
Take this and burn that place down.

51:30.296 --> 51:31.255
What?

51:31.338 --> 51:32.965
Are you out of your mind?

51:33.048 --> 51:34.216
Don't worry about it.

51:34.300 --> 51:37.761
I know the guys inside. I met them
back in my nine-tailed fox days.

51:38.387 --> 51:41.724
Loan sharks, illegal gambling,
organ trafficking, you name it.

51:41.807 --> 51:46.395
This place is crawling with wicked
and evil people doing that kind of stuff.

51:47.021 --> 51:48.772
Trust me, they deserve to die.

51:49.398 --> 51:50.441
Hey.

51:50.524 --> 51:53.152
Didn't you just say
that "one human is a whole world"?

51:53.235 --> 51:55.446
And now you want me
to burn people to death?

51:55.529 --> 51:56.655
What are you talking about?

51:56.739 --> 51:58.407
I'm a very cultivated beast, you know.

51:58.490 --> 51:59.992
Then what's this for?

52:00.075 --> 52:03.287
You start the fire,
then I'll swoop in and put it out in time.

52:03.370 --> 52:05.748
Or we can just call the fire department.
That'd mean I saved

52:05.831 --> 52:08.959
a bunch of lives
in that building all at once.

52:11.003 --> 52:12.546
First the river, now fire?

52:13.380 --> 52:15.382
You really will stop at nothing.

52:16.133 --> 52:18.302
I can't do this. I won't.

52:18.844 --> 52:20.638
Do you honestly think this makes sense?

52:20.721 --> 52:23.015
What's wrong now? Why not?

52:23.098 --> 52:26.185
Jeez, you never just agree to anything.

52:26.268 --> 52:30.689
So you're talking about
a false kindness, aren't you?

52:30.773 --> 52:32.441
The important part is the kindness.

52:32.524 --> 52:33.525
Hey!

52:33.609 --> 52:36.028
You want us to be the bad guys,
not the good guys!

52:36.111 --> 52:39.114
Either way, we're still saving them.
That's all that matters, isn't it?

52:39.198 --> 52:41.367
Don't you know
what happens to the bad guys?

52:41.450 --> 52:43.911
They always end up ruined
and in the gutter.

52:43.994 --> 52:45.245
Enough!

52:45.329 --> 52:47.748
I'm older than any bad guy out there.

52:47.831 --> 52:49.375
So just do as I say.

52:50.000 --> 52:52.461
If you want to start a fire,
do it yourself.

52:52.544 --> 52:53.921
I can't do it.

52:55.464 --> 52:57.508
I would've done it already if I could.

52:57.591 --> 53:00.844
I need to do good deeds,
so I can't do bad things.

53:00.928 --> 53:03.222
Oh, so you know it's bad?

53:03.305 --> 53:04.348
Fire!

53:04.973 --> 53:06.517
Fire!

53:07.851 --> 53:09.103
Did you…

53:09.895 --> 53:10.896
It wasn't me.

53:10.979 --> 53:13.315
It really wasn't. I'm right here.

53:15.693 --> 53:18.320
But where is the fire?

53:30.749 --> 53:33.085
HOPE ORPHANAGE

53:35.045 --> 53:38.090
- Did you call 911?
- Yes.

53:38.173 --> 53:40.884
But the children are still inside!

53:40.968 --> 53:42.594
There are children inside?

53:42.678 --> 53:43.971
Yes.

53:46.473 --> 53:47.891
Here, hold this.

53:49.560 --> 53:51.729
Si-yeol, what are you doing?

53:51.812 --> 53:53.272
You wait here. It's too dangerous.

53:53.355 --> 53:54.481
What?

53:57.443 --> 53:58.360
Si-yeol!

54:16.795 --> 54:19.047
Si-yeol, I can't see a thing.

54:19.131 --> 54:21.508
I told you not to come! It's dangerous!

54:21.592 --> 54:23.218
Come to think of it,

54:23.927 --> 54:26.680
if anyone saves the kids,
it has to be me, not you.

54:26.764 --> 54:29.183
What? Are you crazy?

54:29.933 --> 54:31.101
Cover your face with this.

54:32.478 --> 54:35.314
I think the fire started in the basement.

54:35.397 --> 54:37.691
Let's get the kids out
before it spreads up here.

54:44.823 --> 54:46.533
- Hey, kids.
- Teacher!

54:48.494 --> 54:50.496
Are you all right?

54:51.246 --> 54:52.372
Okay, let's go.

54:55.626 --> 54:57.044
Take the kids and get out first.

54:57.127 --> 54:59.171
I'll check over there,
then follow you out.

54:59.254 --> 55:00.506
I'm scared!

55:01.298 --> 55:02.382
Let's go.

55:16.814 --> 55:18.190
Is that everyone?

55:20.192 --> 55:22.110
I can't find So-jeong!

55:50.305 --> 55:52.057
They're out!

55:53.600 --> 55:55.853
Oh, So-jeong!

56:06.321 --> 56:09.658
Where's the woman I was with?

56:09.741 --> 56:12.369
She went back inside just now.

56:13.036 --> 56:14.121
What?

56:16.957 --> 56:18.584
Why won't this open?

56:19.459 --> 56:21.211
Damn it, open up!

56:49.823 --> 56:51.199
Don't be ridiculous.

56:51.700 --> 56:53.744
You think I'm going to die like this?

57:06.131 --> 57:07.257
Eun-ho!

57:07.799 --> 57:08.800
Eun-ho!

57:08.884 --> 57:09.843
Si-yeol.

57:10.636 --> 57:13.889
Seriously, what are you doing?
Are you trying to get yourself killed?

57:19.353 --> 57:20.854
Eun-ho, are you okay?

57:23.565 --> 57:24.775
Si-yeol!

57:49.091 --> 57:50.926
Oh, you're awake.

57:53.845 --> 57:54.846
What?

57:55.931 --> 57:58.183
Wait, what happened?

58:02.437 --> 58:04.731
Si-yeol. Where is he?

58:05.357 --> 58:06.400
Excuse me?

58:07.442 --> 58:09.361
Wait, ma'am!

58:09.444 --> 58:11.863
- Where are you going?
- Si-yeol!

58:16.702 --> 58:17.703
Si-yeol!

58:22.165 --> 58:23.917
Where is Si-yeol?

58:26.962 --> 58:28.505
You looking for me?

58:31.633 --> 58:33.343
People will think I'm actually dead.

58:33.969 --> 58:36.304
Why are you calling out for me like that?
I'm right here.

58:36.388 --> 58:38.724
I seriously thought you were dead.

58:39.891 --> 58:40.934
Were you scared?

58:42.352 --> 58:43.729
It just so happens that right now,

58:43.812 --> 58:47.065
you're the only person
in the world on my side.

58:47.691 --> 58:50.819
I don't have any friends or family
I can rely on.

58:51.570 --> 58:54.072
You're all I have.

58:54.698 --> 58:57.284
So you should worry about me too.

58:57.367 --> 58:59.244
I'll be worrying about you.

59:02.831 --> 59:03.749
Eun-ho.

59:04.624 --> 59:06.376
You told me to worry.

59:06.877 --> 59:09.463
You said I should worry about you!

59:10.380 --> 59:12.883
I'm really okay, I swear.

59:13.592 --> 59:16.470
Since when do you actually
listen to what I say?

59:31.860 --> 59:35.614
If you had died,
I would've killed you myself!

01:00:16.363 --> 01:00:19.199
NO TAIL TO TELL

01:00:19.282 --> 01:00:20.784
Are you sure you're doing this right?

01:00:20.867 --> 01:00:22.953
We haven't gained
one bit of spiritual power.

01:00:23.036 --> 01:00:24.621
Why isn't the power building up?

01:00:24.704 --> 01:00:28.041
How about we try
doing good deeds by the book?

01:00:28.125 --> 01:00:31.711
What if I stay human
and just die of old age?

01:00:31.795 --> 01:00:35.257
Was there really nothing good
about becoming human?

01:00:35.882 --> 01:00:37.801
Last name Lee, first name Yoon.

01:00:37.884 --> 01:00:39.177
You bastard!

01:00:39.261 --> 01:00:40.262
Kang Si-yeol.

01:00:40.345 --> 01:00:43.014
- He must be a very close friend of yours.
- This memory…

01:00:43.098 --> 01:00:45.183
It is you.

01:00:45.267 --> 01:00:48.353
I know this is all your fault!

01:00:51.565 --> 01:00:53.567
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
